  "client_brief": "Recover our jewellery wordmark from three disagreeing references\n\nMaison Serault has three captures of the existing wordmark and monogram. They disagree in apparent colour and weight. We need a careful reconstruction of the identity, not an average of three photographs.\n\nWhat we need back\n- Maison Serault wordmark: 1 named export. The lettering preserves the authoritative source. Optical spacing is balanced at packaging size.\n- Maison Serault monogram: 1 named export. The approved letter structure is preserved. The mark remains readable at its smallest application.\n- Collection packaging label: 1 named export. The product naming follows the approved collection. The finish treatment respects supplier limits.\n- House stationery application: 1 named export. The brand name is readable. The layout leaves practical writing space.\n\nUse the supplied approved copy and factual records. Permission restrictions in the owner's notes take precedence over inclusion in a source table.\n\nUse the attached brand identity and the source files listed in the asset manifest. The output register defines exact filenames, pages, sizes and record bindings. Supporting previews are welcome but cannot replace those files.",
  "brand_identity": {
    "brand_name": "Maison Serault",
    "tagline": "Worn for years, not seasons",
    "sector": "Independent European fine jewelry house making and selling pieces through its own boutique and a small number of stockists.",
    "founded_place_size": "An independent European house run by its founder, selling from one boutique plus a handful of stockists.",
    "about": "Maison Serault is a small fine jewelry house built around its founder's own hand. Pieces are made and sold through the boutique and a few trusted stockists, and everything leaves in packaging people keep. The house is changing box suppliers, and the new supplier needs proper artwork before it will quote.",
    "personality": [
      "understated",
      "precise",
      "deliberate",
      "warm",
      "unadorned",
      "enduring"
    ],
    "audience": "Buyers roughly 30 to 55 purchasing as a gift or for themselves, plus a small number of stockists. They value discretion and craft over logos.",
    "price_positioning": "Fine jewelry from 600 to 4,000 dollars. Positioned as an independent house: hairline refinement, high contrast, a small mark on a large quiet field, never mass market and never loud.",
    "palette": [
      {
        "name": "Serault Ink",
        "hex": "#1B2A2E"
      },
      {
        "name": "Warm Brass",
        "hex": "#B08D4C"
      },
      {
        "name": "Card Cream",
        "hex": "#EFE9DC"
      },
      {
        "name": "Boutique Charcoal",
        "hex": "#2A2724"
      },
      {
        "name": "Soft Stone",
        "hex": "#C9BEA8"
      }
    ],
    "typography": "A high contrast serif with genuine heritage credibility carries the house name. A quiet companion sets care copy and the address block. Type must never compete with the hairline foil mark.",
    "voice": "Spare, assured, unhurried. A line the house would write: \"Each piece is finished by hand and meant to outlive its first wearer.\"",
    "brand_assets_status": "The working files are gone. The wordmark survives only as one flat export from 2019 whose source files were never sent, a phone photograph of brushed brass letters on the boutique wall, and a daylight photograph of the monogram foil blocked on an old card. The three disagree about the house colour, and there is no vector master of either mark.",
    "values": "Discretion and permanence. A decision made about the mark now sits on packaging for the next ten years, so it has to be right."
  },
  "truth_constraints": [
    "Do not invent names, prices, claims, product features, locations, credentials, records, or documentary events that are absent from the approved inputs.",
    "Do not silently replace a weak supplied asset. Use it honestly, reject it with a reason, or take only the brief's declared Stock or concept exception.",
    "Record every omission, substitution, reconciliation, and material quality compromise in the delivery manifest.",
    "Recover only features supported by the references; do not describe an automatic trace as engraving, cutting, embroidery, or press ready without inspectable path evidence."
  ],
  "production_requirements": [
    "Use the supplied approved copy and factual records. Do not invent claims, prices, dates, credentials or product features.",
    "A clean preview is not a final file. Supply every named export and the separately listed editable source.",
    "Retouching, masks, crop matrices and contact sheets support production; they do not replace the commissioned finished collateral."
  ],
